"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject.TypeModule.add_interface"},{"type":"text","text":"]."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"As long as any instances of these types and interface implementations","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are in use, the module is kept loaded. When the types and interfaces","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are gone, the module may be unloaded. If the types and interfaces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"become used again, the module will be reloaded. Note that the last","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reference cannot be released from within the module code, since that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"would lead to the caller’s code being unloaded before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_object_unref()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"returns to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keeping track of whether the module should be loaded or not is done by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using a use count - it starts at zero, and whenever it is greater than","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"zero, the module is loaded. The use count is maintained internally by","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the type system, but also can be explicitly controlled by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject.TypeModule.use"},{"type":"text","text":"] and [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject.TypeModule.unuse"},{"type":"text","text":"]."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Typically, when loading a module for the first type, "},{"code":"g_type_module_use()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"will be used to load it so that it can initialize its types. At some later","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"point, when the module no longer needs to be loaded except for the type","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementations it contains, "},{"code":"g_type_module_unuse()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GTypeModule"},{"type":"text","text":" does not actually provide any implementation of module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"loading and unloading. To create a particular module type you must"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derive from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GTypeModule"},{"type":"text","text":" and implement the load and unload functions"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"GTypeModuleClass","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModule","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" type acts as a reference-counted owner of an underlying ","type":"text"},{"code":"GTypeModule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It provides the methods that can operate on this data type through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModule","isActive":true},{"text":" as a strong reference or owner of a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GTypeModule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeModuleRef","type":"reference"},{"text